612:const BATCH_INTRO = "This run is climb batch 25, the third batch of the plan's phase 4, the switch-over, and the third of its natives: each library binding builtinPrimitive(\"...\") is to name a static Java helper of nativeHelpers that both paths call, in place of a glue class of walk's, which the compiled path cannot use (P-58; F-32). Climb batches 23 and 24 moved 173 of the 449 live bindings; the count and the distance stand at 0 with them (compile-ladder/climb-batch-24/gate/; F-53). This batch starts N3, the bindings whose helper does not exist yet: each new helper computes as its glue class does. Its rungs: D, Float's 27 bit and rounding operations and the top-level fromRawBits, 28 new helpers; P, RR32's 49, in a new helper class, simpleFloatArith; A, five asFloats declared at RR64, the type of the library's abstract asFloat, two of their helpers new; R, REM and MOD on the five integer types, ten new helpers that raise DivisionByZero at a zero divisor (rows 336 and 848); U, two unsigned helpers and the run time's unsigned printing fixed (rows 326 and 860), the rewrite's NN64 transfer given to UnsignedLong's self, and five bindings moved; N, the integer divisors and nanoTime, 18 new helpers; C, three walls of the code generator, Any in an extends clause, forbid and the test modifier (rows 820, 821 and 823). Every rung that moves bindings writes two guards, a walk program and a compiled program over the same helpers; for a new helper the compiled guard fails before the rung and passes after; and an XXX test for each defect it meets. The planner measured the texts of R, U and A and samples of D, P and N together on this base: the stages 0 and 0; walk's suite 723 tests and two failures, the XXX tests R promotes; the specification's examples 130 and no failure; the compiled tracks one failure, the XXX test U promotes; every value under walk the old code's but the remainders by zero. No rung changes the checker's code, so none makes a speed pass. No rung builds on another, and none lands only with another; the gather applies the rungs in the manifest's order, rewrites the Appendix I entry's Effect once, and runs the 52 team demos on the merged tree; ant testSpecData runs in the gate because the landed summary has it."
